  <dsc><c id="9c57ea2dffd14452f570cbebe5a4ea94" level="series"><did><unittitle>Strategy records</unittitle><unitid>1</unitid><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1242988</unitid><physdesc altrender="whole"><extent altrender="materialtype spaceoccupied">2.66 Cubic Feet</extent><extent altrender="carrier">7 letter size document boxes</extent></physdesc><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="1952/2016" type="inclusive">1952-2016</unitdate></did><scopecontent id="1555ea874372efe3a76b8e1e71a2838a"><head>Scope and Contents</head><p>Series contains an assortment of records that Ford Foundation Program Officer Vanita Nayak Mukherjee created and collected that primarily pertain to the Ford Foundation New Delhi, India Regional Office's sexuality and reproductive health program strategy in India as well as program strategy at the Foundation more broadly. Mukherjee's attendance and participation in various meetings and convenings related to program strategy are documented in materials like agendas, meeting minutes, summaries, correspondence, and notes. </p><p>Much of Mukherjee's work with the New Delhi Office's sexuality and reproductive health programing appears to have aligned with the Foundation's Sexuality and Reproductive Health and Rights unit (SRHR). Documents in the series demonstrate the New Delhi Office's interest in preventing sexual violence, protecting sexual minorities, adolescent sexual and reproductive health and rights, and ending child marriage.  </p><p>Concerning the Ford Foundation's program strategy more broadly, there are materials in the series that document Mukerjee's role as a member of the Foundation's Strategy Advisory Group. There are also records that were created prior to Mukherjee's start at the Foundation that she may have used for training around Foundation practices and procedures for grant making. A significant amount of the materials that originate from before Mukherjee's tenure at Ford appear to have been compiled for the commemoration of the New Delhi Office's 50th anniversary in 2002, including a set of Program Letters authored by Douglas Ensminger, the first Ford Foundation Representative for India. These Program Letters describe Foundation program actions in India and the surrounding countries from as early as the founding of the New Delhi Office in 1952. </p><p>The aforementioned material formats persist throughout the series to document other activities than Mukherjee's attendance at convenings. Additionally, there are drafts, procedure guidelines, tables, and publications.</p></scopecontent><c id="a371178f81db00acf867a851a5975177" level="file"><did><unittitle>Peace and Social Justice Program (PSJ) Worldwide Meeting, New Delhi, India</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1242989</unitid><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="2004/2006" type="inclusive">2004-2006</unitdate><container altrender="Letter Document Box" id="44ec7609c4494c24e2af8b135babd95a" label="mixed materials [A0000000121438]" type="box">1</container><container id="5346a59e1dd28a13ff32e61b93d2cdd0" parent="44ec7609c4494c24e2af8b135babd95a" type="folder">1</container></did></c><c id="84b9196e01faacacb99a299f3d99caa6" level="file"><did><unittitle>Ford Foundation convenings - Various global Sexuality and Reproductive Health and Rights unit (SRHR) meetings</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1242991</unitid><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="2009/2014" type="inclusive">2009-2014</unitdate><container altrender="Letter Document Box" id="43699fbd4d7c788b0dbc5497362f0f99" label="mixed materials [A0000000121438]" type="box">1</container><container id="539c3779291edf4c2bf31ba4d41fd081" parent="43699fbd4d7c788b0dbc5497362f0f99" type="folder">2-3</container></did></c><c id="d2f00bf5caecb6242314e813ceb243a3" level="file"><did><unittitle>Ford Foundation Global Sexuality Research and Advocacy Portfolio convening, Hanoi, Vietnam</unittitle><unitid type="aspace